  "Question": "\\(f(x)=2x+1\\). What is the average rate of change from \\(x=0\\) to \\(x=4\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The average rate of change of a linear function is its slope, 2.\n\nAlternative method 1: Compute endpoint differences\n\nThe average rate of change is the change in function value divided by the change in input. Thus\n\\[\n\\frac{f(4)-f(0)}{4-0}=\\frac{9-1}{4}=2.\n\\]",
